      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1901-09-13_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <p>No. 1170</p>
        <p>COUNTY OF CUES r ER. KNUTSFORD PARLIAMENTARY DIVISION. REGISTRATION OF PARLIAMEN FART ELt.CTnRS, COUNTY ELECTORS, AND PAROCHIAL ELECTORS, 1901.</p>
        <p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, That CLEMENT ii ELPHINSTONE LLOYD, ESQUIRE, having been appointed one of the Barristers to REVISE THE LISTS OF ELECTORS in Parliamentary Elections, within the North Wales Circuit, will make a Circuit and bold Courts for Revising the Lists of Parliamentary Electors, County Electors and Parochial Electors, and also of the separate List of Persons entitled to be elected Members of the County Council of the County ot Chester. though not entitled to be on the County Electors Roll of the said County,for the KNUTSFORD DIVISION of the COUNTY OF CHESTER, at the several times and places following, that is to say On MONDAY, the 23rd day of September next at 11,20 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the National School, Dialey, For the several Parishes in the following Polling Districts, viz. : DISLEY POLLING DISTRICT—D:BI/.7, Lyme Handley. and Newtown. WHALEY BRIDGE POLLING DlSTRlCT—Bettleshulme, Taxall, and Yeardslev-cum-Whaley. On MONDAY, the 23rd day of September next, at 2 45 o'clock in the afternoon, at the News Room, Poyoton, For the several Parishea in the following Polling District, viz. : POYNTON-WITEI-WORTH POLLING DISTRICT—Poynton-witb-Worth and Woodford. On TUESDAY, the 24th day of S ptember next, at 11 45 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the Sunday School. Bollington, for the several Parishes in the following Polling districts, viz .—BOLLINGTON POLLING DlS- TRlCT—Bollington, formerly the Parishes of Bollingron and Berridge, and Pott Shrigley. RAINOW POLLING DlSTRlCT—Macclesfield Forest and Rainow. On TUESDAY, the 24. th day of September next. at 230 o'clock in the Afternoon. at the Black Boy Inn, Preathury- for the several Parishes in the following Polling Districts, viz :—ADLINGTON POLLING DlSTRlCT—Adlington and Newton. PRESTBURY POLLING DISTRICT—ButIey, Fallibroome, Mottram St Andrew, Preatbury, Tytberington and Upton. On WEDNESDAY,the 2btla day ot September next, at 11.30 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the Mill Hall, Wilms- low, for the several Parishes in the following Polling District, viz :—WILMSLOW POLLING DISTRICT— Rollinfee. Styal and Wilmslow. On THURSDAY, the 26:h day of September next, at 11.30 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the Pubic Ball, Alderley Edge, for the several Parishes in the following Polling District, viz :—ALDERLEY POLLING DIS- TRICT—Alderley Edge, Alderley Nether, Alderley Over, Chorley and Warlord Great. On FRIDAY, the 27th day of September next, at 11.15 o'clock in the Forenoon. At the National School, Siddington. For the several parishes in the following Polling District, viz:' SIDDINGTON POLLING DlS- TRlCT—Capesthorn. Chelford. Marton, Siddington, Snelson, S.omerford Booths, Withiogton Lower and , Wallington Old. On FRIDAY the 27th day of September next, at 1 45 o'clock in the Afternoon. At the Club Room of the Bull's Head Hotel, Holmes Chapel. For the several Parishes and parts of Parishes in the following Polling District, viz: HOLMES CHAPEL POLLING DISTRICT— , Brereton-cum-Smethwick, Byley, that part of the Parish formerly known as Byley-cum-Yatehouse ; Church Bulrne, Cotton, Cranage, Davenport, Bermincham, Leese. Somerford, that part of the Parish formerly I known as Somerford-cum-Radnor ; Sproston, that part ,of the Parish formerly known as blooresbarrow-cum- , Parme; Sproston, that pait of the Parish formerly known as Sproston; Swettenisam and Twemlow. On SATURDAY, the 281 h day of September next, at 10.15 o'clock in the Forenoon. At the Sessions Howie, Routsford. Far the several Parishes in the following , Poiling Districts, viz: ASTON-BY-BUDWORTH POLL- ING DISTRICT .93ton-by-Bud g‘orth, Crowley and Pickmere• KNUTSFORD POLLING DISTRICT— Box- ton, Enutsford, Mere, 011erton, Tablev Inferior, Tabley Superior, Tattoos nd Tcft. MOBBERLEY POLLING DIATRICT Muth:al-cum-Watford and Mobberley. I OVER PEOVER POLLING DISTRICT Blackcien. Goostrey-cum-Barnahsw, and Peover Superior. On Monday, the 30;laiday of Si ptembsr next, at 10.30 o'clock in the Forenoon. At the Club Room of the Black Greyhound Inn, Lostock Gralam. For the several Parishes and part of a Parish in the following Polling Districts viz. : ALLOSTOCK POLLING DISTRICT— Allostcck, Peover Inferior and Peover Nether. LOS. TOCK GRAIL AM POLLING DISTRICT—Lach Dennis. Lostock Graham. Plumbley, Rudheath and Whatcroft that part of the Parish formerly known as Shipbrook. On Tuesday,the Ist day of October nett, at 12 o'clock Noon, at the Large Room, Grappenhall. For the several , Parishes in the following Polling Districts, viz. ' GRAPPENBALL POLLING DlSTRlCT—Grappenhall, Latchford Without, and Warrington, that part within the Geographical County of Chester. On Tuesday, the lit day of October next, at 2.15 o'clock in the Afternoon, at the Club Room of the London Bridge Inn, Stockton Heath. For the Several Parishes in the following Polling District, I iz. : APPLE- TON POLLING DISTRICT—Appleton with Hull, Stockton Heath and Stratton. On Wednesday, the 2nd day of October next. at 11.45 o'clock in the Forenoon at the Magistrates' Court house Daresbury. For the several Parishes in the following Polling Districts. viz :—DARESBURY POLLING DIS- TRICT—ActOn Grange, Daresbury, Hatton, Kekewick, Moore, Newton-by-Daresbury, Preston-c:th-Hill. Walton Inferior and Walton Superior. WHITLEY POLLING DISTRIC f;--Antrobus, Seven Oaks, Whitley Inferior and Whitley Superior. And for all and every the Parishes, Townships, and places Of any) within the said Knutsford Division of the County of Cheater, for which Courts to Revise the Parliamentary Electors' Lista County Electors' Lists and Parochial Electors Lists , therein, have not hereinbefore been appointed. At the Courts for such of the above-mentioned Parishes or parts of Parishes as are situate within the Parliamentary Borough of Warrirgton. the Barrister will, under the above Notice, revise the Ownership List only for such Parishes or parts of Parishes. All Overseers and other persons whose attendance may be necessary, are hereby required to attend the said Courts at the several times and places aforesaid, at which the Lists of their respective Parishes are hereby appointed to be revised, and all Overseers are required to produce la Court the Rate Booka of their respective Parishes, containing the Poor Rates made and allowed during the period between the sth day of January, 1900, and tte 15th day of July, 1901, and to bring with them copies of their Lists and all Notices of Claims and Objections, and other Papers they have received, con- cerning the Registration of Parliamentary Electors for i the Knutsford Division and County and Parochial Elec- tors of the said County of Chester. REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Cheshire County Ccuncil, Chester, 21st August. 1901.</p>
