        <p>WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>Musical Successes.</p>
        <p>At the recent examination of the London College of Music the following pupils of the Misses Sutton LuC M, Union Bank Chambers, Market-gate, successfully passed in pianoforte playing, Miss Anastasia Sexton, 85 roarks,lst class with bonoura ; Mit,s Polly Moreton, 89 marks, let class with , honours Theory Elementary : Miss Edith Reddish, 195 marks, Ist class ; Miss Katie Grounds, 93 marks, let class ; Miss Marian England, 89 marks, let class ; Miss Sexton, 85 marks, Ist class ; Miss Ettie Smith, 83 marks, Ist class. Junior Honours Sec- tion : Ist class, Miss Luceika Tutton, also piano- forte playing Senior Divsion Ist class honours. The Coroner's Day's Work.</p>
        <p>Mr Brighouse, county coroner, gtarted from Ormskirk with his clerk at 6 27 a m, on Nlonday,for a full driy'd work, having arranged to hold inquests at St Helens, Eccle4ton, Collins Green, Warrington, Garston, and :Nlaghtill, ten inquiries in all, the last being timed for something past seven in the even- ing Three of the inquest i were held in the evening at ‘Varrington—two at the Police Station and one at the Sloop Hotel, Sankey Bridges.</p>
