        <p>Rescue by a Warrington Man. Mr William Henry Bailey, of Priestley-street was fishing at Preston Brook, on Saturday after- noon, with other Warrington anglers. when his attention was drawn to a drowning boy on the other side of the water. He ran along the bank for some distance, crossed a bridge, ran along the bank on the other side of the water and was just in time to jump in and bring out the lad, who, by this time was in an exhausted condition. The usual methods were adopted and the child soon recovered and was able to return to its home at PrPston Brook.Fouemen stood on the bank near the Child all the time,but made no effort to save its life.</p>
        <p>•</p>
