        <p>RUNCORN UNION —CONTRACTS FOR PRO- VISIONS AND SUPPLIES FOR THB HALF- YEAR ENDING MARCH 29TR. 1902. THE GUARDIANS OF THE POOR OF THE RUNCORN UNION are desirous of receiving TENDERS from parties wining to CONTRACT for the supply of FLOUI,OO.TMBAL: GROCERIES, PEAS. CHEESE, SALT BUTTER; COD LIVER and PARAFFIN OIL ;QUININE; GOOD BEEF. to consist of vein pieces intact. Flat Ribs with Bone, and one Round weekly not to exceed 251bs, and Nibs per week of tne Best Butcher's Meat for the Officers, and Sides of Mutton; BRRAO, HOME-CURED BACON, POIATOES, WHEAT, STRAW, DRAPERY and CLOTHING ; Men's Women's, Boys' and Girls' SHOES of 'carioca sizes, as per samples to be seen at the Workhouse, button, and Shoe Mewling; HOUSE COAL (Collier to be named) Goon DEAL COFFINS, specifying size, .and including Plate With name, age, and date of death to be delivered in the Union when and where required ; COKE; CARTING at per mile FUNERALS at per Funeral. Parties tendering for the supply of the above-mentioned Goods will be required to deliver the same at the Workhouse, free of cost to the Guardiane, how and when required. ; Tenders to be aclompaniecl with samples (except Drapery Goods) as far as practicable The Guardians do not bind them- selves to accept the lowest or any tender. Persons desirous of tendering must apply by letter to my office, in Runcorn, for a prir ted Form of Tender (and none other can be entertained), where a Schedule of the various articles required and further particuiars may be obtained. Sealed Tenders addressed to the Guardian ,to be forwarded to the Clerk's Office. Runcorn. on or before 4ATURDAY, the 21st day of SEPTEMBER. 19(1, endorsed "Tender for" The Tenders will be opened and considered at a Meeting of the Guardians to be held in the Board Room. Dutton, on the 24th day of SEPTEMBER, 1901 at 12-45 p.m. , Parties whose tenders are stocept,ed must enter into a written Contract, and be prepared to enter Into a Bond with two sureties if required by the Guardians. By Order of the Board, alio. F. Astrrolg• Clerk to the Guardians. Runeorn, 2nd September. 1901.</p>
